From: consnop <consnop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:22:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Offer consnop's patched firmware to boards it builds for

consnop/PebbleOS's pipeline branch builds Core's releases with extra
patches and releases them as <upstream tag>-consnop-<patch id>. Watches on
those boards (obelix_pvt) now check that repo instead of Core's releases,
with no fallback to stock builds, so an update never drops the patches.

ReleaseTagVersion ignores suffixes, so the patched check offers a build
whose version is higher, or equal with a different tag: that moves stock
firmware to the patched build of the same version and picks up new patch
builds. Only the newest release is considered, so the running build and
older builds of the same version are never offered.

